e,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.00365,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Autoliv, Inc., through its subsidiaries, develops, manufactures, and supplies passive safety systems to the automotive industry in the Americas, Europe, China, and Asia. The company offers passive safety systems, such as modules and components for frontal-impact airbag protection systems, side-impact airbag protection systems, pedestrian protection systems, steering wheels, inflator technologies, battery cut-off switches, and seatbelts. It also develops and manufactures mobility safety solutions, including passive safety systems for commercial vehicles; and safety solutions for riders of motorcycles and bikes. The company primarily serves car manufacturers. Autoliv, Inc. was founded in 1953 and is based in Stockholm, Sweden.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mikael  Bratt | President, CEO, Member of Research Advisory Board & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 56K people. Revenue per employee of $193K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $13K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $268 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 20\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Autoliv, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $8.7B market cap on $10.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $716M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.57\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 10.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2548929.61},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 21% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Autoliv, Inc. (ALV) is a Top-Ranked Momentum Stock: Should You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029524/autoliv-inc-alv-is-a-top-ranked-momentum-stock-should-you-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3029524","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577803.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Autoliv (ALV) Raises Its Dividend, Is The Stock Still Cheap?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-alv/autoliv/news/autoliv-alv-raises-its-dividend-is-the-stock-still-cheap","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403209.507,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"Is Autoliv (NYSE:ALV) Raising Its Dividend?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/is-autoliv-nysealv-raising-its-dividend","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794401100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Autoliv, Inc. $ALV Position Lowered by Leuthold Group LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/autoliv-inc-alv-position-lowered-by-leuthold-group-llc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794393208.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Autoliv (NYSE:ALV) Declares Increased Quarterly Dividend","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/autoliv-nysealv-declares-increased-quarterly-dividend","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794323640.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Is Autoliv (ALV) Fully Priced After Its Safety Belt Deal?","sou